1. d4 d5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. Bf4 c6
4. e3 { A solid move: it supports d4, and the bishop on f1 can come out. } 4... Bf5 ( 4... Bg4 5. Nf3 e6 6. h3 { Asks the bishop on g4 what it will do. } 6... Bh5 7. g4 { Pushes the bishop back again, and the pawn also gains space. } 7... Bg6 8. Ne5 )
5. Nf3 { Develops toward the centre and guards d4 and e5. } 5... e6
6. Bd3 { Offers to trade Black's good bishop for White's. } 6... Bxd3 7. Qxd3 Nbd7 8. O-O Be7 9. Ne5 { The knight takes a strong central square, backed by the d4 pawn, that Black's pieces cannot easily challenge. } 9... O-O 10. Rfe1 *
